{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Read the retained receipt of experiment 839cb6b70e4745919b7a93c468af5407-experiment (CheckRun e87ee87274544b3ba836dffb93a7ecb1, exit 0, 21 events). The setup event 19 records the restarted node with an empty configuration and outside its own configuration; the result event 20 records that an outsider's AppendEntries was accepted and the outsider became the node's leader, while the node's own campaign control holds. That closes the child question's registered discriminator, so this update consolidates the child account across all of its receipts and adds the matching behavior entry.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n  {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@k-empty-config-leader-admission\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\":\\\"A node whose configuration is empty after a RestoreCommittedLogs restart accepts AppendEntries from a server that appears in no configuration and records that server as its leader, while its own follower loop still refuses to campaign because no peers are known.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"RestoreCommittedLogs=true with a commit-tracking store; no snapshot, so the recovered configuration is empty; the sender is transport-reachable and sends one AppendEntries with a higher term and no entries.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-runfollower\\\",\\\"s-appendentries-stage\\\",\\\"s-restore-committed\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"e87ee87274544b3ba836dffb93a7ecb1\\\":[20]}}\n ],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"7e10640e7212486b94a80f04b69febc2-question-1\\\",\n   \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"839cb6b70e4745919b7a93c468af5407-experiment\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-runfollower\\\",\\\"s-appendentries-stage\\\",\\\"s-restore-committed\\\",\\\"s-commit-tracking-contract\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"e87ee87274544b3ba836dffb93a7ecb1\\\":[19,20],\\\"f418b9d6ab8841faa9ab6c35ce1fcd75\\\":[6,7],\\\"e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75d9\\\":[6,7]},\n   \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Three receipts of the same harness file answer this question: two runs state the vote and pre-vote admission (f418b9d6ab8841faa9ab6c35ce1fcd75 and e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75d9, each at its indices 6 and 7) and this receipt states the AppendEntries and election-gating half (e87ee87274544b3ba836dffb93a7ecb1 at indices 19 and 20). All three start from the same recovery state, an empty configuration after a RestoreCommittedLogs restart.\\\",\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Current account: an empty recovered configuration leaves the node admitting peers that appear in no configuration on both the vote and the leadership paths, while its own participation is gated off. Vote and pre-vote: event 7 of receipts f418b9d6ab8841faa9ab6c35ce1fcd75 and e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75d9 records Granted responses for a candidate absent from every configuration, plus adoption of the requester's higher term, with the live configuration empty and one bootstrapped voter still recorded in the node's log (event 6). Leadership: event 19 of receipt e87ee87274544b3ba836dffb93a7ecb1 records the same empty state, and event 20 records that the outsider's AppendEntries was accepted (success true, response term advanced) and the outsider became the node's recorded leader; that assertion is violated. Gating: the same run's control holds, the node stayed Follower across six heartbeat timeouts and did not campaign on its own, so runFollower's refusal to start an election with no known peers is measured rather than assumed. Mechanism from source: requestVote and requestPreVote apply their membership rejection only when their own Servers list is non-empty, and appendEntries applies no membership check at all, so an empty configuration admits any transport-reachable sender; quorumSize over an empty voter list is 1, which also explains the derived quorum recorded in the earlier probes.\\\",\n   \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n    \\\"The leniency is intentional for a cluster that is being bootstrapped; what makes it a defect here is that the node's own recovery leaves the configuration empty in a cluster that is not being bootstrapped, and the node cannot tell the difference.\\\",\n    \\\"The probe supplied a sender with a higher term and an up-to-date message shape; a sender whose term is stale is still rejected, so the observation is about admission and not about log content.\\\",\n    \\\"The election-gating control holds: the same node does not campaign with an empty configuration, so the failure is asymmetric, admitting others while suppressing itself.\\\",\n    \\\"Any later configuration entry restores the node's configuration, which the parent question's account measures.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"limitations\\\":[\n    \\\"Measured on in-memory single-node clusters with the repository's in-memory transport and commit-tracking store; the sender identity came from the probe rather than from a real election.\\\",\n    \\\"The AppendEntries request carried no entries, so the observation covers accepting leadership only; whether the node would apply entries from that leader follows from the same code path but is not measured.\\\",\n    \\\"The consequence for a live cluster is bounded by the repair path, since the node's configuration is empty only until a configuration entry reaches it.\\\"\n   ]}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
