{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Extended the leader-admission case so the same run also shows whether the outsider's entries reach the node's log and FSM, and queued it as a fresh experiment because the harness bytes changed after the previous receipt. Local construction feedback showed the entry stored and applied; the retained receipt is what the account will rest on.\\\",\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"7e10640e7212486b94a80f04b69febc2-question-1\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-runfollower\\\",\\\"s-appendentries-stage\\\",\\\"s-restore-committed\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"The same single-node empty-configuration restart as the previous case, extended by one phase: after the outsider is accepted as leader, it sends one AppendEntries carrying a single command entry with a commit index covering it, and the probe records whether the entry is stored in the node's log and reaches its FSM.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n    \\\"Cluster, transport, log store and FSM are the repository's own test facilities; snapshotting is disabled so the configuration is empty.\\\",\n    \\\"The outsider remains transport-reachable and its term is the node's current term at the time of the second request.\\\",\n    \\\"The entry is a plain command entry with no configuration semantics.\\\"\n   ]},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Bootstrap a one-node cluster with RestoreCommittedLogs and commit-tracking stores, apply five commands, restart the node with NewRaft on a fresh transport and emit the setup event; sleep six heartbeat timeouts and record state; send an outsider AppendEntries with term+1 and no entries, then send a second AppendEntries from the same outsider carrying one command entry with a leader commit index covering it; wait for the applied index to advance, scan the log store for the payload, and emit the outsider-entries event with the stored flag, the last index and the last applied index before and after.\\\",\n  \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"A node that recovers its configuration from its own log must not store or apply entries sent by a server outside that configuration.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"Raft itself: appendEntries decides whose requests are processed and processLogs decides what reaches the FSM.\\\",\n  \\\"anchors\\\":[\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-appendentries-stage\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"appendEntries\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1458,\\\"end_line\\\":1458}\n  ],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"empty-config-leader-setup\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"empty_config_leader_setup\\\",\n    \\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"live_config_len\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},\n                  {\\\"field\\\":\\\"node_in_own_config\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}]}\n  ],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"empty_config_outsider_entries\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"variant\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"empty-config-leader-setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"entry_applied_from_outsider\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"An entry sent by a server outside the recovered configuration neither is stored nor reaches the FSM.\\\"}\n  ]\n }\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","ex